Subject: winemac: take the foreground back when the application is activated

macdrv_app_deactivated() hands the foreground window to the desktop when the
application is deactivated.  Nothing hands it back.  The return trip relied on
-windowDidBecomeKey, but Cocoa does not send it again on reactivation: a window
that was key when its application was deactivated is still key, so no
WINDOW_GOT_FOCUS is posted and macdrv_window_got_focus never runs.

The application is then left with the desktop as its foreground window for as
long as it runs.  win32u sends WM_ACTIVATEAPP only when the foreground thread
changes, so an application that was told it lost focus is never told it got it
back.  Measured on Super Street Fighter IV, sampling GetForegroundWindow() from
a second process so that reading it did not disturb it:

  foreground -> 001E01D2 SSFIVAE       (playing)
  foreground -> 00010020 #32769        (switched away -- the desktop)
  <nothing, on switching back>

Its DirectInput pad is acquired with DISCL_FOREGROUND, so it goes unacquired on
the way out and, with no WM_ACTIVATEAPP to prompt a re-Acquire, stays that way:
the controller is dead for the rest of the session.

Offer the focus again on activation, so the two halves are symmetric.
---
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
@@ -2172,7 +2172,23 @@
         if (beenActive)
             [self unminimizeWindowIfNoneVisible];
         beenActive = TRUE;
+
+        /* Cocoa does not send -windowDidBecomeKey again when the application
+         * is reactivated: the window that was key when it was deactivated is
+         * still key.  So nothing offers Wine the focus back, and the foreground
+         * macdrv_app_deactivated handed to the desktop is never taken again --
+         * leaving the app with no foreground window and no WM_ACTIVATEAPP.
+         * Deactivation gives it up explicitly; activation has to ask for it
+         * back just as explicitly. */
+        {
+            WineWindow* key = (WineWindow*)[NSApp keyWindow];
 
+            if (![key isKindOfClass:[WineWindow class]])
+                key = [keyWindows firstObject];
+            if ([key isKindOfClass:[WineWindow class]] && ![key isMiniaturized])
+                [self windowGotFocus:key];
+        }
+
